# Joy to the World, the opening (repertoire plan: joy-to-the-world). Lowell Mason's tune Antioch
# (1839) on Isaac Watts's words (1719), in D. Only the carol's first two lines are written here,
# for verses 1 and 2: the part of the tune this arrangement can give note for note.
# Line 1 is the D major scale stepping down an octave, in first position: D (string 2 fret 3),
# C# (string 2 fret 2), B (open string 2), A (string 3 fret 2), G (open string 3), F# (string 4
# fret 4), E (string 4 fret 2), D (open string 4). Rhythm: D quarter, C# dotted eighth, B
# sixteenth | A dotted quarter, G eighth | F# E | D, then "Let" on the last eighth.
# Line 2 climbs back up in pairs, a long note and a short one on the same pitch: B B, C# C#, D.
# The teacher strums D, G and A7.
title: Joy to the World (opening)
id: joy-to-the-world
composer: Lowell Mason (tune Antioch); words by Isaac Watts
source: Words 1719; tune Antioch published 1839; first two lines of verses 1 and 2; arranged for Sixstring Academy
arranger: Sixstring Academy
licence: Public domain (Watts died in 1748, Mason in 1872); this arrangement is original to Sixstring Academy
difficulty: 3
tags: melody, major scale, dotted rhythm, christmas, carol, lyrics
tempo: 72
time: 2/4
key: D

track: Melody
role: lead
